  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.374,
      "end": 2.127,
      "text": "Your bank says the money has left."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.555,
      "end": 4.488,
      "text": "The receiver says nothing arrived."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.9,
      "end": 6.513,
      "text": "So where exactly did your money go?"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.165,
      "end": 8.838,
      "text": "Here's what most people don't realise."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.242,
      "end": 11.688,
      "text": "A bank transfer isn't money jumping between phones."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.074,
      "end": 15.104,
      "text": "An entire payment system works behind that notification."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.745,
      "end": 17.553,
      "text": "When you send to another Nigerian bank,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.656,
      "end": 19.616,
      "text": "your bank initiates the transfer."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.017,
      "end": 23.044,
      "text": "The message moves through Nigeria's interbank payment infrastructure,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.196,
      "end": 26.096,
      "text": "including NIBSS Instant Payment, to the receiving bank."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.717,
      "end": 27.64,
      "text": "But here's the twist."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.707,
      "end": 32.49,
      "text": "A timeout, delayed response or unresolved status can leave both sides"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.57,
      "end": 35.27,
      "text": "with different information. Your account may show a debit,"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.378,
      "end": 38.175,
      "text": "while the receiver's account is not yet confirmed as credited."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.831,
      "end": 40.827,
      "text": "And sometimes the money actually arrived."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.231,
      "end": 42.88,
      "text": "But the SMS alert was delayed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.018,
      "end": 45.81,
      "text": "or never came. That's why an alert alone isn't enough."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.231,
      "end": 48.3,
      "text": "Check the balance and transaction history."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.958,
      "end": 49.688,
      "text": "So what should you do?"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.949,
      "end": 51.906,
      "text": "Don't send the money again."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.941,
      "end": 55.241,
      "text": "Save your receipt and transaction session ID."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.642,
      "end": 60.33,
      "text": "In Nigeria, NIBSS provides a NIP tracker through star five-six-five star five"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.41,
      "end": 63.086,
      "text": "hash, for eligible transfers within 48 hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.496,
      "end": 66.155,
      "text": "If it's successful, the receiver should ask their bank to trace"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.235,
      "end": 68.929,
      "text": "it. If not, contact your bank about the reversal."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.571,
      "end": 71.703,
      "text": "And if your bank doesn't resolve it, escalate."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.119,
      "end": 73.262,
      "text": "Complain to your bank first."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.111,
      "end": 76.742,
      "text": "If unresolved within the applicable two-week period,"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.848,
      "end": 79.66,
      "text": "escalate to the CBN's Consumer Protection Department."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.309,
      "end": 83.591,
      "text": "So next time a transfer says successful but nothing arrives,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.734,
      "end": 85.215,
      "text": "don't just ask where the money went."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.631,
      "end": 87.037,
      "text": "Ask for the transaction trail."
    }
  ]
}
